# Scripts and hooks are checked out with LF on every host (TASK-0262).
#
# WHY: a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows' installer
# default) otherwise writes them CRLF. Git Bash tolerates the carriage
# return, so this repo's gate never saw a problem; a Linux bash does not:
# PowerShell's `bash` is WSL's, and `bash scripts/install.sh` failed there
# at `set -uo pipefail\r` on 2026-11-08. Python is forgiving, but a CRLF
# shebang line is not. The index already holds LF for every one of these,
# so this changes no blob, only the working copy on checkout. Runbook,
# *Line endings on a Windows host*.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
configs/claude-code/hooks/* text eol=lf
